{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rust-lang/rust-analyzer/pulls/23422","id":4645746725,"node_id":"PR_kwDOBttd2s8AAAABFOh4JQ","html_url":"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-analyzer/pull/23422","diff_url":"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-analyzer/pull/23422.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-analyzer/pull/23422.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rust-lang/rust-analyzer/issues/23422","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rust-lang/rust-analyzer/pulls/23422/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rust-lang/rust-analyzer/pulls/23422/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rust-lang/rust-analyzer/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rust-lang/rust-analyzer/issues/23422/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rust-lang/rust-analyzer/statuses/eec72a77e5297eff7a4d6a9a6d1a38339562fc1b","number":23422,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix: don't panic on malformed let-pattern with mismatched or-arm arities","user":{"login":"GauravPawar101","id":144026760,"node_id":"U_kgDOCJWsiA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/144026760?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GauravPawar101","html_url":"https://github.com/GauravPawar101","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GauravPawar101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GauravPawar101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GauravPawar101/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GauravPawar101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GauravPawar101/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GauravPawar101/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GauravPawar101/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GauravPawar101/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GauravPawar101/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**fix crash when a `let` has an invalid or-pattern**\r\n\r\nrust-analyzer crashes on this code:\r\n\r\n~~~rust\r\nlet x: &((S, S),) = ..;\r\nlet ((ref mut r, _) | ((ref mut r, _),),) = &*x;\r\n~~~\r\n\r\nThe two sides of the `|` don't match in shape. The first has two items, the second has one. rustc rejects this as an error (E0308), but we still passed the broken pattern on to the exhaustiveness check, which then tried to read an item that wasn't there and panicked.\r\n\r\n`match` already avoids this by checking that the pattern's types line up before running the check. `let` only did that check on the outermost part of the pattern, so a mismatch buried deeper slipped through.\r\n\r\nNow `let` runs the same full check that `match` does, so invalid patterns are skipped before they can cause trouble. I considered adding another check lower down, in `lower_pat`, but the pattern is already known to be valid by then, so it wasn't needed.\r\n\r\nI added tests, `regression_23336`. It keeps the two type errors in the example rather than hiding them, like the other tests there.\r\n\r\nWhat I ran:\r\n- `cargo test -p ide-diagnostics` and `cargo test -p hir-ty` both pass\r\n- `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo xtask tidy` both pass\r\n- `cargo clippy` \r\n- I reproduced the crash without the fix and confirmed it no longer happens with it\r\n\r\nCloses rust-lang/rust-analyzer#23336","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-26T07:41:37Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T07:59:32Z","closed_at":"2026-10-05T07:59:29Z","merged_at":"2026-10-05T07:59:29Z","merge_commit_sha":"ec5b576b726a1e3d0b860761f0fd73b1665cfa32","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"Veykril","id":3757771,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTc3NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3757771?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Veykril","html_url":"https://github.com/Veykri